    # For medium/short: print "file:line:col: severity[ruleId]: message" plus maybe?
    # We'll look at earlier captures:
    # --report-style=short gave "/tmp/proj2/src/a.py:1:1: warning[r]: hi"
    # --report-style=medium gave "/tmp/proj2/src/a.py:1:1: warning[r]: hi" same?
    # Actually both similar.
    # For rich we need to print file + line preview.
    # For our simple, we will replicate rich as earlier naive: f"{severity}[{ruleId}]: {message}\\n  ┌─ {file}:{line}:{col}\\n  │\\n{line} │ {content}\\n  │ {'^'*len(matched)}"
    # Let's implement.
    if report_style == "rich":
        for r in all_results:
